Recommends:
 systemd,
Description: plugin-based dynamic DNS updater
 Manannan runs as a system service and, on a fixed cadence, reads a value
 from a source plugin (typically the host's public IP address) and
 reconciles it with every record held by one or more registry plugins
 (typically DNS providers). Each record is checked and updated
 independently.
 .
 Included plugins: amazon_check_ip (the public IPv4 address from
 checkip.amazonaws.com) and aws_route53 (A records in AWS Route 53, across
 any number of hosted zones and AWS accounts).
 .
 The service is installed disabled: configure /etc/manannan/manannan.yaml
 and /etc/manannan/environment, then enable manannan.service.

Package: manannan-dev
Architecture: all
Section: libdevel
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 libyaml-cpp-dev,
Description: plugin-based dynamic DNS updater (plugin headers)
 The headers for building Manannan source and registry plugins: the plugin
 interfaces, the descriptor a plugin exports, and the logger it is given.
